        <li>All information is provided "as-is" without warranty of any kind</li>
        <li>You should always consult with a licensed financial advisor before making any investment decisions</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="s3">3. Risk Disclosure</h2>

      <h3>3.1 Trading Risks</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Substantial Risk of Loss:</strong> Trading involves high risk and can result in the loss of your entire investment. Past performance is not indicative of future results</li>
        <li><strong>Leverage Risk:</strong> Many instruments allow leveraged trading, which can amplify both gains and losses</li>
        <li><strong>Market Volatility:</strong> Markets can be extremely volatile, especially during news events, economic releases, or geopolitical events</li>
        <li><strong>Liquidity Risk:</strong> Some instruments may have limited liquidity, making it difficult to enter or exit positions at desired prices</li>
        <li><strong>Overnight Risk:</strong> Holding positions overnight or over weekends exposes you to gap risk from after-hours news or events</li>
        <li><strong>Currency Risk:</strong> Trading international markets exposes you to currency fluctuation risks</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.2 Technology Risks</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>System Failures:</strong> Technical issues, internet outages, or platform failures may prevent you from executing trades</li>
        <li><strong>Indicator Limitations:</strong> No indicator is perfect. Signals may be delayed, incorrect, or fail to predict market movements</li>
        <li><strong>Third-Party Platforms:</strong> We rely on TradingView and Telegram. We are not responsible for failures or changes to these platforms</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.3 Hypothetical Performance Limitations</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Any backtested or hypothetical performance results have inherent limitations</li>
        <li>Hypothetical results do not represent actual trading and may not reflect the impact of market factors such as slippage, liquidity, and execution speed</li>
        <li>No representation is made that any account will or is likely to achieve profits or losses similar to those shown</li>
      </ul>

